# Arduino motor controller, on a Raspberry Pi 3B+.
#
# The same rule as ../pi-3b/99-heron-arduino.rules, with the 3B+'s port
# numbers; ./99-heron-rplidar.rules explains them. Keep the two in step:
#
#   KERNELS "1-1.1.2"   the Arduino (this file)
#   KERNELS "1-1.3"     the LiDAR
#
# Code must open /dev/arduino, never /dev/ttyUSB*.
#
# A replacement board may have a different USB bridge: the bench rig's
# Keyestudio Uno failed on 2026-11-22 (its bridge answered, its ATmega328P
# never did, not even to the bootloader) and the board put in its place
# has a CH340 (1a86:7523). Its line names the same port. The CH340 is not
# the LiDAR's bridge, so it cannot claim /dev/rplidar; only the port tells
# the boards on this robot apart from the LiDAR, as before.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="10c4", ATTRS{idProduct}=="ea60", KERNELS=="1-1.1.2", SYMLINK+="arduino", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7523", KERNELS=="1-1.1.2", SYMLINK+="arduino", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"
